      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The case of a 73-year-old patient whose external cardiac pacemaker produced a constant direct current is reported. The patient had severe angina pectoris, and the ECG showed marked QT prolongation and deformation both of the QRS complex and of the ST-T segments. Both angina and ECG changes disappeared when the defective pacemaker was replaced."},
